1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,580
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:04,980
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:06,150
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,650 --> 00:00:07,540
I've been a locksmith

5
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:08,660
for thirty years.

6
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:10,690
Kneeling at people's front
doors,

7
00:00:10,690 --> 00:00:12,100
all day long.

8
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:13,040
I had my right knee

9
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:14,740
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:17,240
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:18,920
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:20,220
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:21,180
and it went away.

14
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:22,430
This is different.

15
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:22,840
Tight.

16
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:23,520
Full.

17
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:24,510
Like a band around

18
00:00:24,510 --> 00:00:26,240
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:27,230
And for two years

20
00:00:27,230 --> 00:00:28,780
I've been told the same
thing.

21
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:30,050
Give it time.

22
00:00:30,050 --> 00:00:32,650
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:34,250
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:35,060
At three months,

25
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:36,260
give it six.

26
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:37,380
At six months,

27
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:39,100
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:39,740
At a year,

29
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:41,840
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:43,310
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:43,310 --> 00:00:45,060
We went down the list.

32
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:46,730
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:46,730 --> 00:00:47,870
Every session,

34
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:49,630
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:49,980 --> 00:00:51,230
I got stronger.

36
00:00:51,230 --> 00:00:52,690
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:52,690 --> 00:00:54,510
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:54,510 --> 00:00:56,300
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:58,340
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:58,340 --> 00:00:59,390
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:59,390 --> 00:01:00,520
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:02,560
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:04,810
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:04,810 --> 00:01:05,880
And after that, a second

45
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:06,940
operation to go back

46
00:01:06,940 --> 00:01:08,460
in and do it over.

47
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:09,550
I said no.

48
00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:12,380
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:12,380 --> 00:01:13,380
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:15,290
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:15,290 --> 00:01:17,970
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:19,640
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:20,890
for it and went to

54
00:01:20,890 --> 00:01:22,080
my first call.

55
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:23,760
Couldn't do the stairs,

56
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:25,400
couldn't kneel at a
customer's door

57
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:26,550
without grabbing the frame

58
00:01:26,550 --> 00:01:27,860
to get back up,

59
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:29,140
couldn't stand at the
counter

60
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:30,820
long enough to finish
dinner,

61
00:01:30,820 --> 00:01:32,300
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

62
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:34,690
game without shifting
every two minutes.

63
00:01:34,690 --> 00:01:36,160
It woke me at night,

64
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:38,150
and it turned ordinary
things,

65
00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:39,670
like climbing out of the van

66
00:01:39,670 --> 00:01:40,890
or up off the couch,

67
00:01:40,890 --> 00:01:42,190
into a decision.

68
00:01:42,190 --> 00:01:43,370
After a long and serious

69
00:01:43,370 --> 00:01:44,680
talk with my wife,

70
00:01:44,680 --> 00:01:46,940
I went back in one more
time.

71
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:48,100
That was the fourth set

72
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:49,620
of X-rays on this knee.

73
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:50,800
And like the three before
it,

74
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:53,160
the answer was everything
looks great.

75
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:55,180
No loosening, no
infection,

76
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:56,110
nothing wrong.

77
00:01:56,110 --> 00:01:57,660
Only this time there

78
00:01:57,660 --> 00:01:58,720
was no new number.

79
00:01:58,720 --> 00:01:59,930
Nobody said

80
00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:01,170
give it another six
months.

81
00:02:01,170 --> 00:02:03,280
There was nothing left to
give it.

82
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:04,250
I sat in the parking

83
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:05,490
lot for a while.

84
00:02:05,490 --> 00:02:07,090
Okay, I thought.

85
00:02:07,090 --> 00:02:08,710
Then explain this.

86
00:02:08,710 --> 00:02:10,350
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

87
00:02:10,350 --> 00:02:11,640
I hit my breaking point.

88
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:13,900
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

89
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:15,930
Everyone in the house was
asleep

90
00:02:15,930 --> 00:02:17,760
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

91
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:18,870
with my leg up,

92
00:02:18,870 --> 00:02:21,000
trying to find any angle
where

93
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,300
it didn't feel like
something

94
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:23,530
was wrapped around my knee

95
00:02:23,530 --> 00:02:24,640
and tightening.

96
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:27,110
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

97
00:02:27,110 --> 00:02:30,060
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

98
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:31,230
And I just thought,

99
00:02:31,230 --> 00:02:33,160
is this really my life now?

100
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:34,020
I had a full day

101
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:35,400
of calls in the morning.

102
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:37,040
I can't live like this.

103
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:38,990
So I made myself a
promise.

104
00:02:38,990 --> 00:02:40,010
I wouldn't go a day

105
00:02:40,010 --> 00:02:41,820
without looking for an
answer.

106
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:43,330
And when I found one,

107
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:44,590
I'd share it with everyone

108
00:02:44,590 --> 00:02:46,050
going through the same
thing.

109
00:02:46,050 --> 00:02:47,810
So I got my laptop

110
00:02:47,810 --> 00:02:49,200
out and went looking.

111
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:50,490
Not for a product.

112
00:02:50,490 --> 00:02:52,020
For an explanation.

113
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:53,760
Mayo Clinic forums,

114
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:56,100
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

115
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:59,030
doctor videos, medical
animations.

116
00:02:59,030 --> 00:02:59,970
And that's when I found

117
00:02:59,970 --> 00:03:01,610
a video from a physical
therapist

118
00:03:01,610 --> 00:03:02,170
named Dr.

119
00:03:02,170 --> 00:03:04,500
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

120
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,450
had been through exactly
this.

121
00:03:06,450 --> 00:03:08,650
But before I say anything
else,

122
00:03:08,650 --> 00:03:10,170
I want to be straight with
you.

123
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:12,630
You've already had
something work fast.

124
00:03:12,630 --> 00:03:13,690
The ice.

125
00:03:13,690 --> 00:03:15,700
The first week of a new
pill.

126
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:17,340
The good day after a
session.

127
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:19,010
Then it wore off.

128
00:03:19,010 --> 00:03:21,810
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

129
00:03:21,810 --> 00:03:24,000
Fast relief isn't relief.

130
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,290
It's a preview.

131
00:03:25,290 --> 00:03:26,680
So I'm not going to tell

132
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:27,910
you this works fast.

133
00:03:27,910 --> 00:03:29,000
It doesn't.

134
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,680
But if you're willing to
be patient,

135
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:31,430
and to look at what's

136
00:03:31,430 --> 00:03:33,210
going on around your new
knee

137
00:03:33,210 --> 00:03:34,640
instead of inside it,
there

138
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:36,890
is a real reason it still
hurts.

139
00:03:36,890 --> 00:03:38,810
And something you can do
about it.

140
00:03:38,810 --> 00:03:39,940
Let me explain what he
said,

141
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:42,050
because this is what
changed

142
00:03:42,050 --> 00:03:43,330
everything for me.

143
00:03:43,330 --> 00:03:45,300
He started with the
basics.

144
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:46,920
A knee replacement takes
out

145
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:49,050
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

146
00:03:49,050 --> 00:03:50,510
in metal and plastic.

147
00:03:50,510 --> 00:03:52,200
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

148
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:53,890
you had before the
operation.

149
00:03:53,890 --> 00:03:55,490
That part I already knew.

150
00:03:55,490 --> 00:03:57,020
But then he explained
something

151
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:58,620
nobody had ever told me.

152
00:03:58,620 --> 00:03:59,480
He said,

153
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:00,800
think about a swollen foot

154
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:02,110
inside a shoe.

155
00:04:02,110 --> 00:04:03,620
The shoe didn't shrink.

156
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:05,750
Your foot is taking up
more room,

157
00:04:05,750 --> 00:04:07,980
so everything feels
cramped

158
00:04:07,980 --> 00:04:09,890
and tight and squeezed.

159
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:11,300
Your new knee sits

160
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:12,830
in a limited space with
living

161
00:04:12,830 --> 00:04:14,890
tissue packed all around
it.

162
00:04:14,890 --> 00:04:16,760
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

163
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:18,800
had to work through that
tissue.

164
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:21,570
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

165
00:04:21,570 --> 00:04:23,700
At first that's normal.

166
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:25,340
But in some people that
swelling can

167
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:28,260
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

168
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:30,000
And swollen tissue takes
up more

169
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,900
room than calm tissue
does.

170
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:33,270
So when you bend,

171
00:04:33,270 --> 00:04:35,040
that tissue gets
compressed.

172
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:35,970
When you straighten,

173
00:04:35,970 --> 00:04:37,340
it gets pulled tight.

174
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:38,800
That's the band.

175
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:41,280
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

176
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:42,090
And you start being

177
00:04:42,090 --> 00:04:43,180
the one who says,

178
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:43,930
you go ahead.

179
00:04:43,930 --> 00:04:45,090
I'll stay here.

180
00:04:45,090 --> 00:04:46,980
And that's exactly why so
much

181
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:49,390
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

182
00:04:49,390 --> 00:04:51,510
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

183
00:04:51,510 --> 00:04:52,570
around the knee.

184
00:04:52,570 --> 00:04:53,790
Worth doing,

185
00:04:53,790 --> 00:04:54,770
and I'd done it.

186
00:04:55,310 --> 00:04:56,740
It does nothing about
tissue

187
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:57,900
taking up room.

188
00:04:57,900 --> 00:04:59,120
A nerve block quiets

189
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:00,980
the nerve carrying the
signal.

190
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:02,950
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

191
00:05:02,950 --> 00:05:04,320
But when that irritated
tissue

192
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:05,800
finally calms down,

193
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,140
it holds less fluid,

194
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:08,830
and it takes up less room.

195
00:05:08,830 --> 00:05:10,000
Less room taken up means

196
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,770
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

197
00:05:11,770 --> 00:05:13,550
That's what takes the
pressure off.

198
00:05:13,550 --> 00:05:15,160
After two years of this,

199
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:16,890
it finally made sense.

200
00:05:16,890 --> 00:05:18,880
The problem was never the
new knee.

201
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:20,680
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

202
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:22,180
He calls it the squeeze.

203
00:05:22,180 --> 00:05:24,730
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

204
00:05:24,730 --> 00:05:26,650
I'd bought knee sleeves,

205
00:05:26,650 --> 00:05:29,170
compression braces,
creams,

206
00:05:29,170 --> 00:05:30,900
half of Amazon really,

207
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:32,520
and all any of it gave me

208
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:33,640
was an hour.

209
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:34,590
I even looked at going

210
00:05:34,590 --> 00:05:36,560
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

211
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:38,110
But at $200 a session

212
00:05:38,110 --> 00:05:39,890
with nothing covered by
insurance,

213
00:05:39,890 --> 00:05:41,440
that was a quick no.

214
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:42,690
Then one night I went

215
00:05:42,690 --> 00:05:43,910
back to that knee
replacement

216
00:05:43,910 --> 00:05:45,870
group and actually read
it.

217
00:05:45,870 --> 00:05:47,270
Thousands of people,

218
00:05:47,270 --> 00:05:48,980
years out from surgery,

219
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:52,070
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

220
00:05:52,070 --> 00:05:53,530
nobody could explain.

221
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,770
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

222
00:05:55,770 --> 00:05:58,080
the same thing kept coming
up.

223
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:59,520
This one device,

224
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:01,330
and people saying it was
the first

225
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:02,850
thing that made a
difference.

226
00:06:02,850 --> 00:06:04,490
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

227
00:06:04,490 --> 00:06:05,370
alright, here it comes,

228
00:06:05,370 --> 00:06:06,340
he's selling me something,

229
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:08,370
let me shut that down
right now.

230
00:06:08,370 --> 00:06:09,970
I'm only here because I
made myself

231
00:06:09,970 --> 00:06:12,120
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

232
00:06:12,120 --> 00:06:13,060
that if I ever found

233
00:06:13,060 --> 00:06:14,230
something that helped,

234
00:06:14,230 --> 00:06:15,300
I'd say so.

235
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:16,690
It's called the KenRelief
Red

236
00:06:16,690 --> 00:06:18,310
Light Therapy Wrap.

237
00:06:18,310 --> 00:06:20,400
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

238
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:21,450
It looked like the cheap

239
00:06:21,450 --> 00:06:22,840
knee sleeves off Amazon

240
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,570
that did nothing for me.

241
00:06:24,570 --> 00:06:26,070
But I went to their
website anyway,

242
00:06:26,070 --> 00:06:27,050
just to see what all

243
00:06:27,050 --> 00:06:28,480
the fuss was about.

244
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:30,660
It's the same red light
therapy

245
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:33,010
clinics charge $200 a
session

246
00:06:33,010 --> 00:06:34,900
for, off machines that
cost

247
00:06:34,900 --> 00:06:36,310
fifty thousand dollars,

248
00:06:36,310 --> 00:06:37,290
in a wrap you plug

249
00:06:37,290 --> 00:06:38,570
into the wall at home.

250
00:06:38,570 --> 00:06:40,380
Two hundred and forty
lights.

251
00:06:40,380 --> 00:06:42,310
Red at 660 nanometers

252
00:06:42,310 --> 00:06:45,080
and near-infrared at 850,

253
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:47,610
run together for the
strongest effect.

254
00:06:47,610 --> 00:06:49,220
Four strength levels.

255
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:51,440
A five to thirty minute
timer.

256
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:53,280
Then I saw the guarantee.

257
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:54,520
Ninety days.

258
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:56,220
Results or your money
back,

259
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:58,750
no questions, no store
credit,

260
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:00,860
and you don't even send it
back.

261
00:07:00,860 --> 00:07:03,160
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

262
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,880
days to change my mind.

263
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:06,340
There wasn't much to lose,

264
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:07,700
so I ordered it.

265
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:09,120
Two of them, actually.

266
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:10,990
Only the right knee was
replaced,

267
00:07:10,990 --> 00:07:12,790
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

268
00:07:12,790 --> 00:07:14,830
and I'd done it for two
years.

269
00:07:14,830 --> 00:07:17,570
The left one was carrying
the difference.

270
00:07:17,570 --> 00:07:18,570
When it came,

271
00:07:18,570 --> 00:07:20,790
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

272
00:07:20,790 --> 00:07:22,160
because I'd been let down
too

273
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:23,950
many times to get excited.

274
00:07:23,950 --> 00:07:25,460
What I felt was warmth.

275
00:07:25,460 --> 00:07:27,320
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

276
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:28,900
More like it was coming
from inside

277
00:07:28,900 --> 00:07:30,530
the knee and spreading
around it.

278
00:07:30,530 --> 00:07:31,630
And that was it.

279
00:07:31,630 --> 00:07:33,520
That was the whole
experience.

280
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:34,820
When I took it off,

281
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:36,000
I'll be honest,

282
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,450
nothing dramatic had
happened.

283
00:07:38,450 --> 00:07:40,460
And after what that video
said,

284
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,700
that's exactly what I
expected.

285
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:43,510
What was different

286
00:07:43,510 --> 00:07:45,500
was that for the first

287
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:47,020
time in two years

288
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:48,820
I'd done something for my
knee

289
00:07:48,820 --> 00:07:50,170
instead of to it.

290
00:07:50,170 --> 00:07:51,230
Twenty minutes,

291
00:07:51,230 --> 00:07:52,570
in my own chair.

292
00:07:52,570 --> 00:07:54,350
No drive, no copay.

293
00:07:54,350 --> 00:07:55,810
They say twenty minutes.

294
00:07:55,810 --> 00:07:56,520
I did thirty,

295
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:57,370
twice a day,

296
00:07:57,370 --> 00:07:59,390
lowest setting that first
week.

297
00:07:59,390 --> 00:08:00,920
I put it on the calendar,

298
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,480
